  "verses": {
    "verse": [
      [
        "Shall we gather at the river,",
        "where bright angel feet have trod;",
        "with its crystal tide forever",
        "flowing by the throne of God?"
      ],
      [
        "On the margin of the river,",
        "washing up its silver spray,",
        "we will walk and worship ever,",
        "all the happy golden day."
      ],
      [
        "Ere we reach the shining river,",
        "lay we every burden down;",
        "grace our spirits will deliver,",
        "and provide a robe and crown."
      ],
      [
        "At the smiling of the river,",
        "mirror of the Saviour's face,",
        "saints whom death will never sever",
        "lift their songs of saving grace."
      ],
      [
        "Soon we'll reach the shining river,",
        "soon our pilgrimage will cease;",
        "soon our happy hearts will quiver",
        "with the melody of peace."
      ]
    ]
  },
  "arrangerNotes": "Verified against the soprano line of the Wikipedia LilyPond SATB score. Slurred notes are written separately. No accidentals. Range 1 to high 1, minLayout 8. Medium because of the dotted eighth-sixteenth rhythms. C and D arrangements use identical degree sequences (both fit their drums). Lyrics of the added verses: Verses 2–5: Robert Lowry (1864) as printed in The Army and Navy Hymnal (1920), from Wikisource (https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/The_Army_and_Navy_Hymnal/Hymns/Shall_We_Gather_at_the_River). The refrain is sung after every verse.",
  "verified": true
